oded  leaving second-degree burns over 20% of  his body even after a three day  medically induced coma the pain was so  bad that curry contemplated suicide in  response Curry's comedian friends  particularly Sinbad jumped into action  they talked with curry on the phone and  were generally just there for him in an  effort to lift his spirits  curry later spoke with people  magazine about his journey out of the  ordeal revealing that Sinbad making him  laugh was one of the things that lifted  his spirits Sinbad is still a touring  comic but if he's gracing a stage these  days it's far more likely that he's  doing it as a musician after buying a  drum kit and learning to play a couple  years back he formed a band for the  first time in more than 30 years it's a  jazz funk group called Memphis red and  the stank nasty band  Sinbad fronts the group singing and  playing guitar under the stage name of  his alter ego Memphis red musical  performances as Memphis red happened to  bookend Sinbad's 2014 comedy special  make me wanna holla hopefully his funk  starts influencing his comedy and  vice-versa if it hasn't already in  December 2009 the IRS went after Sinbad  for millions in uncollected taxes he  apparently hadn't paid federal income  tax in about a decade  it was so bad that a judge ordered that  he sell as 1.5 million dollar house in  Hidden Hills California  to help alleviate some of the eight  point 1 5 million dollars he owed the  government to protect himself he filed  for chapter 7 bankruptcy but the case  was later dismissed because he filled  out the wrong paperwork  regardless Sinbad was still on the hook  for his crushing tax debt and he ended  up filing for bankruptcy again in 2013  around that time he explained that his  financial problems were not a result of  squandering my fingers I didn't live  under live large I believed in me I  invested in me and I'm invested in a lot  of other people I would not change it I  would not go back a year after filing  